// ============================================================================
// EXPORT CONTRACT — DOCUMENTATION ONLY. THIS FILE IS NEVER COMPILED.
//
// src/pipeline/run-souffle.sh includes only the five phase directories
// (projections, containment, resolution, expression-resolution,
// call-edge-generation). engine/export/ is deliberately outside that loop, and
// export_manifest.tsv is the ONLY source of .output directives. Putting a
// `.output` here does nothing — which is exactly the trap this comment exists to
// close.
//
// ── call-chain-edges.csv  (call_chain_edge) ─────────────────────────────────
// THE primary export. No header row (souffle writes none), tab-separated, 7 columns:
//
//   0 Site        the call site. A py_call_site's CALL-expression hash, or — for a
//                 decorator application, which is a call the parser records in a
//                 different relation — the decorator's expression hash (or the
//                 decorator hash when it has no expression node).
//   1 Caller      the enclosing method. NEVER blank: module-level code is owned by
//                 the synthetic <module> MODULE_INITIALIZER and class-body code by
//                 <classbody> (schema §4.2). A "-" here means the parser's
//                 guarantee broke, and is emitted on purpose so it is visible.
//   2 ToExpr      "-" — reserved for expression-level linkage. Kept so the column
//                 count matches Java's call_chain_edge exactly.
//   3 Callee      a py_method hash (Prov=client), a lib_py_method hash (Prov=lib),
//                 a `builtin:NAME` label (Prov=builtin), or "-" (unresolved).
//                 THE LABEL IS DELIBERATELY NOT HASH-SHAPED: no such entity exists
//                 in any IR, and it must be impossible to mistake for an FK.
//   4 Prov        client | lib | builtin | -
//   5 EdgeStatus  known_edge | multi_inferred | boundary_lib | ambiguous_unknown
//   6 Kind        the schema's own callKind (SIMPLE_CALL, METHOD_CALL, SELF_CALL,
//                 SUPER_CALL, CHAINED_CALL, DECORATOR_CALL, DYNAMIC_CALL, ...) or
//                 DECORATOR_<kind> for a decorator application.
//
// CONSERVATION IS THE CONTRACT. Every row of py_call_site and every row of
// py_decorator appears at least once as column 0. test/python/tools/coverage_guard.py
// asserts it against both inventories, and test/python/ci-conservation.sh gates on it
// independently of the goldens — because a golden file full of correct edges is
// perfectly consistent with an engine that quietly discards what it does not
// understand, and that engine reports excellent precision.
//
// ── the four tiers, and what each one PROMISES ──────────────────────────────
//   known_edge         exactly one resolved client target.
//   multi_inferred     a SOUND set: the true target is among them. Only three rules
//                      may produce it, each with a stated argument —
//                      self-dispatch over constructed subclasses, a multi-write
//                      attribute's write union, and two incomparable MRO definers
//                      where C3's tie-break would decide. Nothing else widens a site.
//   boundary_lib       the callee is named and outside the analysed code.
//   ambiguous_unknown  a declared blind spot, with a reason in
//                      call-site-unresolved.csv.
//
// ── the companion exports ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
// call-site-unresolved.csv    every blind spot WITH ITS REASON. A blind spot you can
//                             name is a work item; one you cannot is a mystery.
// call-chain-summary.csv      the tier counts and the site total — the conservation
//                             ledger as data, so the invariant is queryable.
// resolution-mro-position.csv the ORDERED linearisation, where the engine's
//                             precedence order is total. resolution-mro-tie.csv is
//                             where it is not, i.e. exactly where this engine is less
//                             precise than real C3.
// crosscheck-*.csv            agreement with the parser's own (run-local)
//                             pre-resolution. Measured, not assumed.
// lib-link-missed.csv         calls whose written dotted path names something outside
//                             the client that no import link explained — the size of
//                             python-library-linking's remaining work, as a number.
// ============================================================================
